## PT-001 — BUG STANDARD: Fix check-architecture.sh False Positives
Date: 2026-06-24
Status: CLOSED
Branch: fix/PT-001-check-architecture-sh
Objective: Fix CI architecture check failing on every push due to false positives from auto-generated files and missing email function exclusions
Root cause: grep pattern `<[a-z][a-z0-9]*[^>]*>` matched TypeScript generics (Array<string>, Omit<X,Y>) and Astro reference directives (/// <reference types="astro/client" />) in .astro/ cache dirs and env.d.ts files. Additionally, send-delivery-email and send-status-email excluded from Rule 2 but not Rule 1.
Solution: Added --exclude-dir=".astro", --exclude="*.d.ts", --exclude-dir="send-delivery-email", --exclude-dir="send-status-email" to Rule 1 grep. Added "Omit<\|Array<" to grep -v filter. Added --exclude-dir=".astro" to Rule 2 grep. check-architecture.sh now exits 0.
Modified files:
  - src/scripts/check-architecture.sh (Rules 1 and 2)
  - .gitattributes (*.sh text eol=lf — commit 8ebe656)
  - src/scripts/check-architecture.sh rewrite to find|xargs (BusyBox compat — commit 73354ae)
Evidence: docs/implementation/evidence/PT-001/
Delta: Validation revealed 2 additional bugs: (1) CRLF line endings on Windows caused bash failure in Docker; (2) BusyBox grep in Alpine does not support --include/--exclude-dir flags, causing silent false-pass. Both fixed in subsequent commits on main.
Validation: Human confirmed EXIT 0 in Docker Alpine container (bash -c "cd /workspace && bash src/scripts/check-architecture.sh"). 2026-06-24.
PTSA reference: H-001 CERRADA

