## PT-004 — BUG STANDARD: TOTP Secret Encryption
Date: 2026-06-24
Status: CLOSED
Branch: fix/PT-004-totp-encryption
Objective: Fix plaintext TOTP secrets in profiles table — security regression vs encrypted payment_credentials
Root cause: profiles.totp_secret TEXT stored TOTP seeds in plaintext. payment_credentials.credentials_encrypted BYTEA uses pgcrypto AES-256. Inconsistency exposed auth secrets in DB backups and logs.
Solution: Migration 00039: ALTER profiles.totp_secret TEXT → BYTEA (encrypted). Created save_totp_secret_secure() and get_totp_secret_secure() DB functions (pgp_sym_encrypt/decrypt, AES-256, ENCRYPTION_KEY passed as transaction-local parameter — same pattern as migrations 00028/00029). Updated setup-totp (write via RPC), confirm-totp and verify-totp (read via RPC). ENCRYPTION_KEY validated at runtime (≥32 chars). Added 4+4 contract tests for confirm-totp and verify-totp.
Modified files:
  - src/supabase/migrations/00039_encrypt_totp_secret.sql (NEW)
  - src/supabase/functions/setup-totp/index.ts (RPC write)
  - src/supabase/functions/confirm-totp/index.ts (RPC read)
  - src/supabase/functions/verify-totp/index.ts (split profile select + RPC read)
  - src/supabase/functions/confirm-totp/__tests__/confirm-totp.test.ts (NEW)
  - src/supabase/functions/verify-totp/__tests__/verify-totp.test.ts (NEW)
Evidence: docs/implementation/evidence/PT-004/
Delta: Migration 00039 used (00038 was used by PT-005). Existing totp_secret values NULLified rather than encrypted (pre-production safe — no real enrolled vendors). Production would need an out-of-band migration script.
Validation: Human confirmed `SELECT data_type FROM information_schema.columns WHERE table_name='profiles' AND column_name='totp_secret'` → `bytea`. Migration 00039 applied in local Supabase DB (Docker). 2026-06-24.
PTSA reference: H-006 CERRADA

